# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.pipeline (M4-S3).
#
# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. The repo is 5.2 GB on disk and 3.5 GB
# of that is data/ (2.0 GB of DVC-pinned parquet) plus .venv/ (1.5 GB of wheels
# the image resolves for itself). A build without these exclusions ships both to
# the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# Rule of thumb for anything added later: the image may contain CODE, CONFIG and
# the LOCKFILE. Data reaches tasks at run time (M4-S4's decision: MinIO or a
# mounted path), never by being baked in — data is DVC's to pin, and an image
# carrying a copy of it would be a second, unpinned definition of the dataset.

# --- the two big ones ---
data/
.venv/

# --- host-resolved state the image must rebuild, not inherit ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dvc/cache/
dist/
*.egg-info/
mlruns/

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances, in an image layer ---
.env
.env.*

# --- history, run logs and editor state: no bearing on what the image runs ---
.git/
.github/
automation/logs/
automation/runs/
analytics/dbt/target/
analytics/dbt/logs/
analytics/dbt/dbt_packages/
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb
analytics/dbt/marts.duckdb.wal
.idea/
.verify_m1_sandbox/
notebooks/
